[Rank 3] Title: IBM z/Transaction Processing Facility Enterprise Edition Identify a document in a filtered collection
URL: https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/ztpf/1.1.2025?topic=mongodb-identify-document-in-filtered-collection
Score: 0.09438126534223557
Content: Identify a document in a filtered collection   
   In standard  MongoDB , a unique ID is required to be associated with a document in a collection. For unfiltered collections, the ObjectId value represents the unique ID.  
 The _id field for documents in filtered collections is the filtered ID. The filtered ID includes the ObjectId value, index name, and algorithm string. The filtered ID is the default _id format that is used for documents in filtered collections. You can use the _id field that is returned on a query request to locate and access a document on a subsequent request for a filtered collection. 
   The following example shows the _id field of a document in the filtered collection: 
_id : {
         {oid:  objectIdValue ,   
          idx:  IndexName ,
          alg:  algorithmstring }
         }
     objectIdValue   The objectId value or the  z/TPF  file address that is used to access the document.  
     IndexName   The name of an index element that is used to locate the filtered collection. 
 algorithmstring   The algorithm string that is built from the index specification to locate the filtered collection.  
     If the collection is filtered on variable data, the filtered ID must be used to uniquely identify documents in the filtered collection. In this case, do not specify the optional idType attribute in the  z/TPFDF collection descriptor  or set the idType attribute to  FilteredID .  
 If the collection is filtered on fixed data, the objectId value is sufficient to uniquely identify a document. In this case, you can set the idType attribute in the  z/TPFDF collection descriptor  to either  FilteredID  or  ObjectID . If you set the optional idType attribute to  ObjectID  in the  z/TPFDF collection descriptor , the _id field for documents in the collection contains only the objectId value, which is the same as documents in unfiltered collections.
