Content: tpf_STCK_to_timet: Convert tpf_TOD_type to time_t   
 This function converts a  z/TPF  time-of-day (TOD) stamp to time_t format. You can format or manipulate the return from this function with any standard C function that is defined in the  time.h  header file. 


Last updated      Changed in  2023 . 
 Added for  PUT04 . 


Format    #include  <tpf/tpfapi.h>
time_t   tpf_STCK_to_timet(tpf_TOD_type tod);         tod   A TOD clock value of type tpf_TOD_type. 


Normal return    A time_t representation of the specified TOD. 


Error return    None. 


Programming considerations    The TOD clock will overflow after 17 September 2042 at 23:53:47. As a result, the TOD clock value that the STCK and STCKF instructions return will wrap to a value that is zero or close to zero. If the wrapped TOD clock value that is zero or close to zero is specified for the  tpf_STCK_to_timet  function, the function treats the value as 1 January 1900, or shortly after, and returns a negative time_t value. #include <tpf/c_stck.h>

tpf_TOD_type tod;

// The following time_t value represents 23:53:48 on September 17, 2042,
// which is the first time_t value after the TOD clock rollover
time_t timet = 2294610828;

// Converting this time_t value to a TOD stamp will result in the
// following TOD clock value: 0x0000000099B00000, which corresponds
// to the year 1900.
tod = tpf_timet_to_STCK(timet); 
   To avoid this problem, investigate the use of the extended TOD clock with the  tpf_STCKE_to_timet  and  tpf_timet_to_STCKE  functions. #include <tpf/c_stcke.h>

tpf_TOD_ext_type tod;
time_t timet = 2294610828;

// Using the extended function for the conversion will result in the
// following TOD clock value: 0x010000000099B000. The first byte is the
// epoch value, which indicates that the TOD clock has rolled over once.
tpf_timet_to_STCKE(timet, &tod);
