 def  jobName = jobExec.getSubmittedJobName()
 def  listDDNames = jobExec.getAllDDNames( true )

jobExec.saveOutput( new  File( "/u/usr1/jcl/output.txt" ))
   Example 5:  Encode and save output as ASCII. 
 jobExec.saveOutput( new  File( "/u/usr1/jcl/output.txt" ),  "ISO8859-1" )
   Note:  The  saveOutput  API uses  iconv  to convert output from the JES spool. When no target codepage is provided, or the target and source are the same,  iconv  is not used, and output will be           saved in its original encoding. You can specify both source and target encodings by using the following format: 
 saveOutput​(String ddName, File file, String sourceEncoding, String targetEncoding)
   sourceEncoding : The source encoding of output provided by the JES spool. When no source encoding is provided, or the value is null, the codeset provided by  nl_langinfo  will be used, with a fallback to  IBM-1047 . 
 targetEncoding : The target encoding  iconv  will use to write the output. 
 Example 6:  Override default wait time. 
 JobExec.execute()  uses a default wait time of 1 hour before it returns unsuccessfully if a job has not finished. This wait time can be overridden by specifying a length and unit of time. 
 import  java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;

 // Wait up to 30 minutes 
jobExec.execute( 30 , TimeUnit.MINUTES)

 // Wait up to 12 hours 
jobExec.execute( 12 , TimeUnit.HOURS)

 // Wait up to 1 day 
